  "worked_solution": "Let us call $B$ the event \"the black bag is chosen\" and $N$ the event \"a  ball labeled $N$ is drawn.\" \n\nThe required probability is $P(B\\cap N),$ which is given by\n\n$$\nP(B\\cap N)=P(B)\\cdot P(N|B).\n$$\n\nLet's find $P(B)$ and $P(N|B).$\n\n- There is $1$ black bag among the $2$ bags, so we have\n\n$$\nP(B)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n- There is $1$ ball labeled $N$ among the $4$ items in the black bag. So, we have\n\n$$\nP(N|B)=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above data into the multiplication law for conditional probability, we get\n\n$$\nP(B\\cap N)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$",
